<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.10.3: Comparing Functions Represented in Separate Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01027</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.10.3: Comparing Functions Represented in Separate Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a6a955cb-441a-47b2-8faf-4824b0d0be2d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>The number of people who watched a TV episode is a function of that show’s episode number. Here are three graphs of three functions—\(A\), \(B\), and \(C\)—representing three different TV shows.</para>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-align-items-center">
  <para>Show A <figure><media alt="10 data points on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6d75be6f085a2a634ee4183036bf1fc22c2a49c5"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>Show B <figure><media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a1912e552a2554e03bb918a73b6894555e02e6c1"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>Show C <figure><media alt="10 data points on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c1cfd27f7b441df073cac25a4cd34a31c1a89ddc"/></media></figure></para>
</div>


<para>Match each description with a graph that could represent the situation described. One of the descriptions has no corresponding graph.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="solution" data-content-id="05e5ac70-69ae-4ca7-b9a1-ba65f1dad1a0" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--pulldown-->
  <exercise data-content-id="55e82363-cfbc-47ef-9686-e02aaf346a67" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="graph of function C" data-solution-options="[&quot;graph of function A&quot;, &quot;graph of function B&quot;, &quot;graph of function C&quot;, &quot;no match&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>This show has a good core audience. It had a guest star in the fifth episode that brought in some new viewers, but most of them stopped watching after that.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph of function \(C\)</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="3d080c5a-8054-479a-9f61-4bd9fa4b3120" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="no match" data-solution-options="[&quot;graph of function A&quot;, &quot;graph of function B&quot;, &quot;graph of function C&quot;, &quot;no match&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>This show is one of the most popular shows, and its audience keeps increasing.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! no match</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="bfa3a562-185d-4ba8-b510-49dbc5bb5223" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="graph of function A" data-solution-options="[&quot;graph of function A&quot;, &quot;graph of function B&quot;, &quot;graph of function C&quot;, &quot;no match&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>This show has a small audience, but it’s improving, so more people are noticing.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph of function \(A\)</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="3c5faec7-0e76-4ed2-a378-ea37bb6269a1" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="graph of function B" data-solution-options="[&quot;graph of function A&quot;, &quot;graph of function B&quot;, &quot;graph of function C&quot;, &quot;no match&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> This show started out huge. Even though it feels like it crashed, it still has more viewers than another show.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph of function \(B\)</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="074f8390-8547-4d20-a6b1-175f0c152fbf" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="B(7)" data-solution-options="[&quot;A(7)&quot;, &quot;B(7)&quot;, &quot;C(7)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which is greatest, \(A(7)\), \(B(7)\), \(C(7)\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(B(7)\)</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
